 "text": "Hey, how's your day been so far? A sketch is a quick and rough drawing you do first, often just pencil lines. A study is detailed drawing you do before a painting, so you know what you' doing. Kind of, though it' more fun than that. It helps you work out the composition and detail. Lovely. For the sky, would you paint one flat layer, or build it up with gradients? The basic shape of the mountain range, the horizon line, and the shape of the hill you're standing on. Clouds are tricky. One flat layer usually works, but gradients can give them texture. Try rubbing out part of it.",
